
### version
$ devnet-dvpn version
devnet-dvpn 0.1.0  network devnet  linux
(exit 0)

### help
$ devnet-dvpn help
devnet-dvpn — pure-P2P dVPN on the Sentinel Solana devnet

Usage: devnet-dvpn <command> [args] [--json] [--yes]

Overview
  version
      App version, network, program and mint.
  status
      Wallet, device, service and session at a glance.
  logs [--lines N]
      The app log, secrets removed.
Wallet
  wallet show
      Address and balances (SOL, tDVPN, refundable, approved).
  wallet receive
      Address with a QR code.
  wallet create --yes
      New 24-word wallet; prints the phrase once.
  wallet import <file|-> --yes
      Import a phrase, key file or base58 secret.
  wallet send --to <address> [--tdvpn N] [--sol N] --yes
      Send tDVPN or SOL.
  wallet logout --yes
      Remove the wallet from this computer.
Device + spending permission
  device show
      Device key, spending limit, token permission, device SOL.
  device plan [--allowance N]
      What setup would sign (no transaction).
  device setup [--allowance N] --yes
      Approve tokens, add the device as operator, send it fee SOL.
  device register [pubkey]
      Adopt an existing service device key.
  device revoke --yes
      Remove this device's spending permission (other devices keep theirs; the shared token approval stays).
VPN service (dvpnd)
  daemon version
      Service build and network.
  daemon doctor
      Service health checks (ok / warn / fail).
  daemon drivers
      WireGuard, AmneziaWG, OpenVPN, nftables, DNS: ready or missing (no admin).
  daemon repair-drivers --yes
      Install or repair missing VPN drivers (one admin prompt).
  daemon init
      Create the device key (no admin needed).
  daemon install --yes
      Install and start the service (one admin prompt).
  daemon settings
      Kill switch, DNS, LAN, RPC (key hidden).
  daemon set [--kill-switch off|on|persist] [--dns handshake|cloudflare|ip,ip] [--dns-mode resolvectl|resolvconf|none] [--allow-lan true|false] [--basis per_gb|per_hour] [--escrow tDVPN] [--prepay-mb N] [--prepay-minutes N] [--rpc URL] [--rpc-ws URL] --yes
      Change service settings (admin prompt, restarts it).
  daemon restore-network
      End any session, release kill switch and proxy.
Servers
  nodes list [--online] [--country DE] [--protocol wireguard] [--sort price] [--no-probe]
      Every listed server, checked live.
  nodes show <node>
      One server: prices, protocols, signature checks.
  nodes fav <node>
      Add or remove a favourite.
  nodes recent
      Servers you used most recently.
  cost <node> [--basis per_gb|per_hour] [--units N]
      Exact deposit before you connect.
Connect + sessions
  connect <node> [--basis per_gb|per_hour] [--units N] [--plan <subscription>] [--switch] --yes
      Pay a deposit (or use a plan) and connect.
  connect <node> … --follow
      Connect, then print usage every 5 s.
  disconnect
      Stop the session; the deposit settles later.
  sessions
      Sessions the service holds.
  tickets
      Plan access tickets the service holds.
  proxy status
      SOCKS endpoint and system-proxy state.
  proxy on --yes
      Point desktop apps (GNOME/KDE system proxy) at the session SOCKS proxy.
  proxy browser [--browser chrome|chromium|edge] [--url U]
      Open Chrome, Chromium or Edge in its own profile through the session (only that window uses the VPN).
  proxy off
      Restore your own proxy settings.
Plans + subscriptions
  plans list
      Every plan on the network.
  plans roster <plan>
      Servers on a plan, live or down.
  plans subscribe <plan> --yes
      Buy a plan (no refund).
  plans subscriptions
      Your subscriptions and time left.
  plans close <subscription> --yes
      End a subscription (rent back, no refund).
Deposits, refunds, history
  channels
      Deposits the service holds.
  channels fund <channel> --tdvpn N --yes
      Top up a deposit that is still open.
  settle list
      Deposits waiting to be refunded.
  settle run [--channel C] --yes
      Start / finish closing deposits.
  settle withdraw --yes
      Move refunds back to the wallet.
  history list
      Every session with data and spend.
  history summary
      Totals, last 30 days, top servers.
  history export [--out file.csv]
      Session history as CSV.
Node testing
  test plan <node…> | --online
      Most a test run could lock in deposits (no transaction).
  test run <node…> | --online [--max-spend N] --yes
      Real session on each server, one at a time: connect time, exit IP, DNS, speed → FAST / SLOW / FAIL. Test deposits are closed after.
  test stop
      Stop a running test after the current server (it disconnects first). Ctrl-C does the same in the terminal running it.
  test history
      Past test runs with FAST / SLOW / FAIL counts.
  test show [run-id] [--compare]
      One run per server (latest if no id); --compare shows what changed since the run before.
  test export [run-id] [--out file.json]
      A run as JSON.
Diagnostics
  quality ip
      Public IP as websites see it.
  quality speed
      Download speed test.
Settings + RPC
  rpc state
      Endpoint in use, slot, latency (key hidden).
  rpc set <url> [url…]
      Your own Solana RPC endpoints (https).
  poll show
      Background refresh cadences: current, default and allowed range for each job.
  poll set <job>=<seconds> …
      Change how often a background job runs (wallet, nodes, plans, subscriptions, settlements, ip, dns, rpc, session).
  poll reset [job…]
      Put cadences back to their defaults.
  poll run [job…]
      Run background jobs once now and show how long each took.
  poll watch [--seconds N] [--hidden]
      Run the real scheduler for N seconds and check every job kept its cadence (exit 1 if not).
  settings get
      App settings.
  settings set key=value …
      Change app settings (unknown keys refused).

Env: DVPN_KEYFILE (use a key file in place), DVPN_DATA_DIR, DVPN_DAEMON_SOCKET, DVPN_DAEMON_HOME, DVPN_DAEMON_TARGET=host:port
(exit 0)

