### wallet logout needs --yes
$ devnet-dvpn wallet logout
Remove the wallet key from this computer. Funds stay on chain; you need your backup to get back in.
Re-run with --yes to do it.
(exit 2)

### wallet send needs --yes
$ devnet-dvpn wallet send --to 9enW4xCJrmytnEC6VsJYPbcT2ng3QTUwUkAHSrKR9Xrj --sol 0.001
Send 0.001 SOL to 9enW4xCJrmytnEC6VsJYPbcT2ng3QTUwUkAHSrKR9Xrj on Solana devnet.
Re-run with --yes to do it.
(exit 2)

### wallet send rejects a bad address
$ devnet-dvpn wallet send --to nope --sol 0.001 --yes
"nope" is not a Solana wallet address.
(exit 3)

### wallet send needs an amount
$ devnet-dvpn wallet send --to AFaCESaEAFHZZCg6uzPvShVALUuACJnSh3i2wBe14kWB
Give --tdvpn N and/or --sol N.
(exit 3)

### wallet logout --yes
$ devnet-dvpn wallet logout --yes
Wallet removed.
(exit 0)

### logout removed the keyring entry
$ bash -c ! secret-tool search --all application devnet-dvpn 2>/dev/null | grep -q '/home/ubuntu/ddv-sweep-local'

(exit 0)

